WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.01
This is journey seven of Hewn, the software factory: cancel a direction.

00:00:06.01 --> 00:00:09.83
Sometimes the work in progress is simply not wanted any more.

00:00:09.83 --> 00:00:13.77
An Owner needs to stop it quickly, keep what is already merged,

00:00:13.77 --> 00:00:16.65
and leave a clear mark on anything still open.

00:00:16.65 --> 00:00:21.03
This video walks through how it was built: the flow, the control poll,

00:00:21.03 --> 00:00:25.48
the cancel itself, the labelled pull requests, the page, and the tests.

00:00:26.63 --> 00:00:32.26
An Owner presses Cancel on a running or paused direction, and confirms in a dialog.

00:00:32.26 --> 00:00:37.15
The active run stops within ten seconds, and the direction is Cancelled.

00:00:37.15 --> 00:00:41.22
Open pull requests stay open, with the label hewn cancelled.

00:00:41.22 --> 00:00:45.02
If another direction is waiting in the queue, it starts.

00:00:45.02 --> 00:00:49.43
Viewers never see the control, and the API answers four oh three.

00:00:50.58 --> 00:00:52.12
Here is the whole flow.

00:00:52.12 --> 00:00:56.99
While a run executes, the worker holds a control request open to the API.

00:00:56.99 --> 00:01:02.33
When the Owner confirms, the API labels the open pull requests, cancels the run,

00:01:02.33 --> 00:01:07.87
the stage and the direction, and starts the next queued direction, all in one save.

00:01:07.87 --> 00:01:09.94
Then it wakes the held request.

00:01:09.94 --> 00:01:14.95
The worker hears Cancel, stops the step in progress, and the dialog closes.

00:01:16.10 --> 00:01:21.10
Workers only ever call out to Hewn, so a Local worker needs no open port.

00:01:21.10 --> 00:01:26.71
To hear a cancel within seconds, the worker keeps one request open while it works,

00:01:26.71 --> 00:01:28.42
twenty seconds at a time.

00:01:28.42 --> 00:01:32.88
The API answers the moment the run is cancelled, or with nothing,

00:01:32.88 --> 00:01:34.66
and the worker asks again.

00:01:35.01 --> 00:01:39.69
On the API side, the poll checks that this worker still holds this run.

00:01:39.69 --> 00:01:44.18
If the run is still leased, it waits for a signal, then looks again.

00:01:44.18 --> 00:01:48.53
A cancelled run is answered with Cancel, and the stop is recorded.

00:01:48.88 --> 00:01:53.56
In the worker, the Cancel answer aborts the step in progress at once.

00:01:53.56 --> 00:01:56.95
No further step, checkpoint or result is reported.

00:01:58.10 --> 00:02:00.78
The cancel command takes the project's lock.

00:02:00.78 --> 00:02:05.85
It sends a Direction cancelled event, writes Cancel requested by, into the run log,

00:02:05.85 --> 00:02:07.62
and labels the pull requests.

00:02:07.62 --> 00:02:11.71
Then the orchestrator cancels the run, its stage and the direction,

00:02:11.71 --> 00:02:13.97
and starts the next queued direction.

00:02:13.97 --> 00:02:16.54
Only after saving does it wake the worker,

00:02:16.54 --> 00:02:19.10
and wait up to ten seconds for it to hear.

00:02:19.10 --> 00:02:24.17
If the worker never answers, the direction is Cancelled anyway: its lease no longer

00:02:24.17 --> 00:02:25.57
lets it write anything.

00:02:26.72 --> 00:02:28.81
Which pull requests are open?

00:02:28.81 --> 00:02:33.71
The mutation ledger already records every pull request a run opened.

00:02:33.71 --> 00:02:38.98
Each one that is not merged gets the hewn cancelled label through GitHub,

00:02:38.98 --> 00:02:43.01
and the run log shows the matching g h p r edit command.

00:02:43.01 --> 00:02:44.81
Merged work stays merged.

00:02:45.96 --> 00:02:50.26
On the project page, Owners see Cancel beside Pause or Resume.

00:02:50.26 --> 00:02:54.82
It opens a confirmation dialog: Keep running, or Cancel direction.

00:02:54.82 --> 00:02:58.98
While Hewn waits for the worker, the button says Cancelling.

00:02:59.33 --> 00:03:04.43
If the worker has stopped answering, the dialog names it, and offers Try again.

00:03:04.43 --> 00:03:08.17
The page behind says the worker hasn't confirmed the stop,

00:03:08.17 --> 00:03:11.01
and that Hewn refuses anything more from it.

00:03:11.01 --> 00:03:15.92
The cancelled page says who cancelled and when, how quickly the run stopped,

00:03:15.92 --> 00:03:18.76
and which pull request is open and labelled.

00:03:18.76 --> 00:03:21.15
It works in dark mode and on a phone.

00:03:22.30 --> 00:03:25.08
Each slice began with its tests failing.

00:03:25.08 --> 00:03:30.70
The backend gained seven tests against the real API: stopping a running direction

00:03:30.70 --> 00:03:35.56
within ten seconds, a worker that does not answer, a paused direction,

00:03:35.56 --> 00:03:41.39
the next queued direction, the labelled pull request, the Viewer, and the conflicts.

00:03:41.39 --> 00:03:46.32
The worker gained five tests against a fake API and a real HTTP server.

00:03:46.67 --> 00:03:50.39
All green, the backend has one hundred and eighty five tests,

00:03:50.39 --> 00:03:55.32
the worker one hundred and thirty eight, and the frontend seventy one unit tests.

00:03:55.32 --> 00:03:58.85
End to end, three new pipeline tests cancel a real worker.

00:03:58.85 --> 00:04:03.72
One checks the stop within ten seconds and the labelled pull request in the fake

00:04:03.72 --> 00:04:08.83
GitHub, one checks that the queued direction starts, and one stops the worker first,

00:04:08.83 --> 00:04:10.35
to see the failed dialog.

00:04:10.35 --> 00:04:12.78
There are fifty end to end tests in all.

00:04:13.93 --> 00:04:16.92
Here is a direction running Detailed designs.

00:04:16.92 --> 00:04:21.62
Its Scaffold stage opened pull request number one, which is still open.

00:04:21.62 --> 00:04:25.40
The Owner presses Cancel, and the dialog asks to confirm.

00:04:25.40 --> 00:04:26.53
Cancel direction.

00:04:26.53 --> 00:04:29.05
Cancelling, while the worker hears it.

00:04:29.05 --> 00:04:31.03
Then the page shows Cancelled.

00:04:31.03 --> 00:04:35.74
The log reads Cancel requested, the label command for pull request one,

00:04:35.74 --> 00:04:36.80
and Run stopped.

00:04:36.80 --> 00:04:40.05
The callout says the run stopped within a second.

00:04:40.40 --> 00:04:45.09
In the fake GitHub, pull request number one is still open, not merged,

00:04:45.09 --> 00:04:47.56
and carries the hewn cancelled label.

00:04:47.91 --> 00:04:52.10
Now a second project, with a feature direction waiting in the queue.

00:04:52.10 --> 00:04:57.15
The Owner cancels the running direction, and the feature direction starts straight

00:04:57.15 --> 00:04:59.24
away, with its Idea stage running.

00:04:59.59 --> 00:05:05.00
And when the worker has gone silent, the dialog says Cancel didn't reach the worker,

00:05:05.00 --> 00:05:06.99
names it, and offers Try again.

00:05:06.99 --> 00:05:11.05
A Viewer sees the cancelled direction, with no controls at all.

00:05:12.20 --> 00:05:14.02
Journey seven is complete.

00:05:14.02 --> 00:05:17.30
Cancel stops the active run within ten seconds,

00:05:17.30 --> 00:05:19.89
over a request the worker holds open.

00:05:19.89 --> 00:05:23.66
Open pull requests stay open, labelled hewn cancelled,

00:05:23.66 --> 00:05:26.25
and the next queued direction starts.

00:05:26.25 --> 00:05:28.07
And only Owners can do it.

00:05:28.07 --> 00:05:31.91
Next comes journey eight: stop and restart all workers.
